    "result": "Perfect! \u2705 The frai-core test suite is now fully passing with all 28 tests across 8 test files.\n\n## Summary of fixes\n\nI fixed two issues in the source code:\n\n1. **`src/finetune/index.js`** - Added named exports for the schema constants (`APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, `RISK_LEVELS`) so they can be imported directly, while maintaining the default export for backward compatibility.\n\n2. **`src/eval/metrics.js`** - Fixed the toxicity metric in `DEFAULT_METRICS` by wrapping it to ignore the references parameter. The issue was that `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`, but `toxicityMetric` was incorrectly interpreting references as banned terms, causing all outputs to be flagged as toxic.\n\nAll public exports remain intact and functional.",
